---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import Article from '../../components/Article.astro';
import { getDict } from '../../i18n/dictionaries';
import { SITE, breadcrumbJsonLd, guideHreflang } from '../../lib/seo';
const dict = getDict('en');
const title = 'Sound-Measurement Guide Hub';
const description = 'Learn to measure, calibrate and interpret browser sound levels: how the meter works, accuracy, calibration, decibel chart and privacy.';
const url = `${SITE}/guides/`;
const jsonLd = [breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: 'Home', url: `${SITE}/` }, { name: 'Guides', url }])];
const items = [
  { href: '/how-to-use/', t: 'How to use the online decibel meter', d: 'Permissions, placement, reading the panel and exporting sessions.' },
  { href: '/methodology/', t: 'How browser sound measurement works', d: 'Microphone access, local processing, RMS, dBFS, weighting, Leq.' },
  { href: '/calibration/', t: 'How to calibrate a browser decibel meter', d: 'Reference equipment, placement, offsets, profiles and mistakes.' },
  { href: '/accuracy/', t: 'Browser decibel-meter accuracy and limitations', d: 'Hardware variation, AGC, mobile vs desktop, certified meters.' },
  { href: '/decibel-chart/', t: 'Decibel comparison chart', d: 'Approximate everyday sound levels from 30 to 120 dBA.' },
  { href: '/db-vs-dba/', t: 'dB vs dBA: weighting explained', d: 'A, C and Z weighting plus Fast and Slow response.' },
  { href: '/microphone-not-working/', t: 'Microphone troubleshooting', d: 'Denied, missing, busy or disconnected inputs.' },
  { href: '/privacy/', t: 'Microphone and audio-processing privacy', d: 'Local processing, permissions, storage and hosting.' },
  { href: '/microphone-noise-floor-test/', t: 'Microphone noise floor test', d: 'A 30-second raw dBFS diagnostic with no simulated readings.' },
  { href: '/background-noise-test/', t: 'Background noise test', d: 'A focused room-noise workflow that respects calibration state.' },
  { href: '/dbfs-vs-db-spl/', t: 'dBFS vs dB SPL', d: 'Why digital level and physical sound pressure have different reference points.' },
  { href: '/noise-exposure/', t: 'Noise exposure and hearing safety', d: 'Level plus duration: NIOSH bands, the 3 dB rule and personal checks.' },
  { href: '/phone-decibel-meter/', t: 'Using your phone as a decibel meter', d: 'Placement, iPhone and Android differences, best practices and limits.' },
  { href: '/frequency-analyzer/', t: 'Frequency analyzer guide', d: 'Reading the live spectrum: bass, speech and hiss as you measure.' },
  { href: '/sound-level-meter/', t: 'What is a sound level meter?', d: 'Hardware classes versus browser estimates, and when each one fits.' },
  { href: '/faq/', t: 'Frequently asked questions', d: 'Short answers on accuracy, calibration, Leq, privacy and safe levels.' },
  { href: '/tone-generator/', t: 'Browser tone generator', d: 'Play pure test tones with frequency, waveform and channel controls.' },
  { href: '/speaker-test/', t: 'Speaker test', d: 'Verify channels and polarity and hunt rattles with a sweep.' },
  { href: '/hearing-age-test/', t: 'Hearing age test', d: 'Screening check for your highest audible pitch. Not a diagnosis.' },
  { href: '/noise-exposure-calculator/', t: 'Noise exposure calculator', d: 'Daily dose from any average level and duration, no microphone needed.' },
];
---

<Layout locale="en" dict={dict} title={`${title} — Real Decibel Meter`} description={description} path="/guides/" hreflang={guideHreflang('guides')} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Article title={title} intro="One hub for every sound-measurement guide: start with the working meter, then go deeper where you need it." reviewed="2026-09-16" breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }]}>
    <p class="mt-2">You get the most from this hub by starting with a live reading, then picking one follow-up. Open the meter, grant permission once per origin, set the phone down with the mic uncovered, and watch current, minimum, Leq, maximum and duration settle over 30–60 seconds. If the number surprises you, the sections below point to the single guide that answers your next question — no account, no download, current Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari over HTTPS.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {items.map((g) => (
        <a href={g.href} class="panel-raised p-4 focus-ring block hover:opacity-90" style="border-radius:10px">
          <h2 class="font-semibold text-[15px] text-white">{g.t}</h2>
          <p class="text-sm mt-1">{g.d}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-white font-semibold mt-6">Which guide answers your question</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">First reading done and unsure what it means? Follow <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/how-to-use/">how to use the meter</a> for placement, Fast 125 ms versus Slow 1 s, and reading the five stats plus the 240-point graph. Number looks plausible but you need it tied to real sound? <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/calibration/">Calibration</a> walks through a same-spot offset against a known reference, why profiles stay device-specific, and when to redo them. Wondering where any browser number comes from? <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> traces permission, mono Web Audio capture with gain processing requested off, RMS to weighted dBFS plus the nominal +100 dB offset, and why idle input shows "--" instead of a simulated low.</p>
    <h2 class="text-white font-semibold mt-6">When your readings feel wrong</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">Two phones disagreeing by 8 dB in the same room is normal before calibration — capsules, gain and cases differ that much. <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/accuracy/">Accuracy</a> maps the floor below roughly 30 dBA where rooms read high, clipping near 95–100 dBA, weak bass, and why whole numbers beat decimals. No bar moving at all? <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/microphone-not-working/">Microphone troubleshooting</a> covers denied permission, busy or missing inputs and disconnected headsets. Quiet-room number stuck high? The raw-input checks in <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/microphone-noise-floor-test/">microphone noise floor test</a> and <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/background-noise-test/">background noise test</a> separate self-noise from real sound, while <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/dbfs-vs-db-spl/">dBFS vs dB SPL</a> explains why negative digital figures and room levels share a name but not a reference.</p>
    <h2 class="text-white font-semibold mt-6">Putting numbers to use without overclaiming</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">Everyday comparisons belong on the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/decibel-chart/">decibel comparison chart</a> from near 30 to 120 dBA, with <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/db-vs-dba/">dB vs dBA</a> sorting A, C and Z picks from the dominant band. Time-weighted thinking lives in <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/noise-exposure/">noise exposure</a> and the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/noise-exposure-calculator/">noise exposure calculator</a>: 85 dBA across 8 hours, halving time per 3 dB, calm below roughly 70 dBA, screening only with formal calls left to Class 1 or Class 2 hardware. Phone-specific placement sits in <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/phone-decibel-meter/">using your phone as a decibel meter</a>, spectrum reading in <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/frequency-analyzer/">frequency analyzer guide</a>, and data handling in <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/privacy/">privacy</a> — local sessions capped at 20, CSV or JSON with dB values only when calibrated, usage-only analytics.</p>
    <p class="mt-4"><a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/#measure">Open the online decibel meter →</a></p>
  </Article>
</Layout>
